# Build context filter for the BACKEND image (build context = repository root).
#
# This matters here: the build context is the whole repository, which contains a
# live .env holding a real Clerk secret key and database password, a populated
# .venv, and frontend/node_modules. Nothing below is needed to run the API, so
# none of it should ever reach the Docker daemon.

# --- secrets and local environment -----------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# --- frontend --------------------------------------------------------------
# This image is backend-only. Excluding this keeps node_modules (hundreds of MB)
# out of the context; the frontend has its own image built from ./frontend.
frontend/

# --- stray / superseded artifacts ------------------------------------------
# The API is served as src.main:app, so the duplicate root main.py is unused.
# NOTE: src/leaderboard_api_project/ must NOT be excluded -- uv_build builds the
# project from it during `uv sync`.
main.py
recovery/
ck*

# --- VCS and Docker plumbing -----------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml

# --- docs and editor cruft -------------------------------------------------
# README.md is deliberately re-included: `uv sync` builds this project via
# uv_build, which reads `readme = "README.md"` from pyproject.toml.
*.md
!README.md
